      "valueBlockBytes": 9522,
      "status": "CORRECT",
      "sourceLine": 14,
      "specificReview": "The complete transparent value retains actual sourceRemainder at b except at b^2<=T/2 with noninterior y+b; there it uses p=a-y when a<=y+b and p=-a-y otherwise. With a>0 these wall-crossing alternatives cannot both hold, and failure of the upper guard plus noninteriority forces the lower crossing. Initial strict interiority makes the chosen p have the same sign as b and |p|<=|b|. The exact future-energy expression remains inside the qualified actual sourceRemainder.",
