      "valueBlockBytes": 0,
      "status": "CORRECT",
      "sourceLine": 67,
      "specificReview": "All branches of the full source proof were read. Small strict-interior steps use hSmall at b and P_b<=Pi, costing C*A. At a small crossing Pi>=1. Upper crossing gives 0<a-y<=b; lower gives 0<a+y<=-b. Consequently each projected p satisfies p^2<=b^2<=T/2 and y+p lies exactly on its selected wall, inside the CLOSED domain of hSmall. Applying hSmall at p and P_p<=2 gives the explicit projected K-bound. Qualified unit50 own-negative-budget theorems, with all probability, interiority, positive-time, smallness, K>=0 and actual old differentiability hypotheses supplied, yield |R_p|+max(-O,0)<=K*|b|^3. Pi>=1 pays this as 2*C*A. The complementary strict-large branch T/2<b^2 uses the qualified unit51 actual large-step bound40*A with all raw halfline reflection, reachability and regularity premises supplied. Since A>=0 and C>=0, all branches are bounded by (2*C+40)*A. Ring normalization restores the exact stated q^3*D^3*Pi. The complete actual type retains the full universally quantified CLOSED-domain hSmall, actual old DifferentiableAt, both positive-time raw reflection identities, and reachable zero-energy equality.",
