    "Equality hits |y+b|=a are crossings because the survival domain is strict. The selected projected displacement equals the hitting displacement, the signed overshoot has delta=0, and both definitions use the same branch.",
    "At b^2=T/2 the small branch is used. The large branch uses the strict complement T/2<b^2. At b^2=T, hzero is passed to unit51 to justify the reachable interior zero-energy future.",
    "At an upper crossing, old strict interiority gives b>=a-y>0. At a lower crossing, -b>=a+y>0. Thus the upper-priority selector never chooses a wall with the wrong orientation; simultaneous upper/lower crossings would contradict a>0.",
    "The projected point is on the CLOSED interval boundary, so the full hSmall interface applies at either wall. Its projected future energy is at least T/2>0. No future-point differentiability or membership in a remaining-label set is silently required.",
    "C=0 is covered: no step divides by C or K, and the own-negative-budget interfaces permit K=0. b=0 is a small strict-interior step and hSmall supplies its zero right-hand side. T>0 ensures the actual Gaussian scaling is well-defined.",
    "Both P_b summands are at most1 for interior terminal z. Envelope nonnegativity supplies A>=0 and crossing Pi>=1 supplies the projected cubic payment. The exact constant2*C+40 dominates C,2*C,40 for C>=0.",
    "Arbitrary nu is restricted by the explicit probability/regularity/reflection/Taylor premises; existence or identification of a Brownian nu is not proved or assumed as a new axiom."
  ],
